jvm_linux: guard the SIGCLD table entry

The signal-name table lists "CLD" alongside "CHLD". SIGCLD is the System V
alias, which glibc provides and bionic does not, so the array initialiser fails
to compile and takes the rest of the file with it:

  jvm_linux.cpp:157:17: error: use of undeclared identifier 'SIGCLD'
  jvm_linux.cpp:182:19: error: invalid application of 'sizeof' to an incomplete
      type 'struct siglabel[]'

Wrap it in #ifdef the way the neighbouring SIGSTKFLT and SIGSYS entries already
are. Nothing is lost on android: SIGCLD is only ever the same number as
SIGCHLD, and that entry is right below it.

diff --git a/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/jvm_linux.cpp b/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/jvm_linux.cpp
index ba84788..c22281f 100644
--- a/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/jvm_linux.cpp
+++ b/hotspot/src/os/linux/vm/jvm_linux.cpp
@@ -154,7 +154,9 @@ struct siglabel siglabels[] = {
 #ifdef SIGSTKFLT
   "STKFLT",     SIGSTKFLT,      /* Stack fault.  */
 #endif
+#ifdef SIGCLD
   "CLD",        SIGCLD,         /* Same as SIGCHLD (System V).  */
+#endif
   "CHLD",       SIGCHLD,        /* Child status has changed (POSIX).  */
   "CONT",       SIGCONT,        /* Continue (POSIX).  */
   "STOP",       SIGSTOP,        /* Stop, unblockable (POSIX).  */
